From: Ilya Vysotsky <il.mohoff2016@yandex.ru>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 03:11:23 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Windows 10 Mobile: a page's popup opens as a tab

window.open with features made a popup window, which on a phone's one
screen sat over the browser; a sign-in with Google stopped at its last page
(accounts.google.com/gsi/transform) and never got back to the site. A
page's popup from a normal browser window is now a foreground tab next to
its opener, as on Chrome for Android: window.close() closes it and the
opener's tab comes back. An app's popups keep their windows.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 chrome/browser/ui/navigator/browser_navigator.cc | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/navigator/browser_navigator.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/navigator/browser_navigator.cc
index debd48b34d2486594c91fddaa42061e87916af0e..98b050c4aa8f751864e0bedf529e098365303bb5 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/navigator/browser_navigator.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/navigator/browser_navigator.cc
@@ -556,6 +556,20 @@ base::WeakPtr<content::NavigationHandle> Navigate(NavigateParams* params) {
     return nullptr;
   }
 
+#if defined(VENETIUM_W10M)
+  // Windows 10 Mobile: a phone shows one window. A page's popup (window.open
+  // with features: a sign-in with Google, a payment) opens as a tab next to
+  // its opener, as on Chrome for Android, and its window.close() closes the
+  // tab and brings the opener's back. As popup windows over the browser, a
+  // sign-in stopped at its last page (accounts.google.com/gsi/transform) and
+  // never got back to the site. An app's popups keep their windows.
+  if (params->disposition == WindowOpenDisposition::NEW_POPUP &&
+      params->app_id.empty() && source_browser &&
+      source_browser->is_type_normal()) {
+    params->disposition = WindowOpenDisposition::NEW_FOREGROUND_TAB;
+  }
+#endif
+
   // Block navigation requests when in locked fullscreen mode. We allow
   // navigation requests in the webapp when locked for OnTask (only relevant for
   // non-web browser scenarios).
